    {
      "id": "claim_42d7b48a7cbf4ad0b87111bb5baacb3a",
      "statement": "afterEngagement (shared by every engagement action and Forget) invalidates the learned/suggestions/articles query keys plus, off the Priority route, every other loaded by-id article, then refetches the article by id with staleTime 0; on the Priority route it only patches the loaded row's score in place and sets the 'Ranking changed' flag when the refetched score differs, never invalidating or refetching the priority list itself, which means an unloaded row whose score has since risen is not surfaced until the user manually refreshes (the documented D-09 staleness tradeoff).",
